<title>EGYPT: Egypt says buys 22,000 tonnes palm oils.</title>
<headline>Egypt says buys 22,000 tonnes palm oils.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Egypt's state-owned Holding Company for Food Industries said it bought on Wednesday a total 22,000 tonnes of palm stearin and palm oil of Malaysian or Indonesian origin for delivery in August.</p>
<p>Moharram Ghanem, head of the sales sector, told Reuters he had bought the oils from Felda in the following lots:</p>
<p>-- 15,000 tonnes of palm oil at $534.5 per tonne.</p>
<p>-- 7,000 tonnes of palm stearin at $416 per tonne. The firm had originally tendered for 10,000 tonnes of stearin.</p>
<p>Ghanem said all prices were C+F.</p>
<p>-- Miral Fahmy +202 578 3290/1</p>
